The documentation website (index.html, news.html, and guide/) loads
GoatCounter's count.js (https://www.goatcounter.com/, ISC License) for
cookieless, privacy-friendly visitor analytics. count.js is vendored into this
repository at assets/count.js (its ISC license header retained) and served
same-origin from the docs site. The website also loads the Cloudflare Web
Analytics beacon from static.cloudflareinsights.com. These counters are docs
site assets only — they are not part of the distributed Python package, and
the observra library itself phones home to nothing.

The documentation website loads Mermaid (https://mermaid.js.org/, MIT License)
from the jsDelivr CDN at runtime to render diagrams. Mermaid is not vendored or
redistributed in this repository or in the distributed package; only the public
docs site references it (pinned to an exact version with a Subresource
Integrity hash).

